<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> AlCl<sub>3</sub>                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.01&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> H<sub>3</sub>BO<sub>3</sub>                                             </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.01&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>MoO<sub>4</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O                             </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.01&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH.  Then proceed to add minerals.  Adjust final pH to 7.0.       <br>
<I>Fe NTA solution:</I> <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NaHCO<sub>3</sub>                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.64&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Nitrilotriacetic acid trisodium salt monohydrate        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.75&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> FeCl<sub>3</sub>&#183;6H<sub>2</sub>O                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.7&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Firstly, dissolve NaHCO<sub>3</sub> in 80 ml distilled water. Then, add nitrilotriacetic acid trisodium salt and FeCl<sub>3</sub>&#183;6H<sub>2</sub>O to the solution, and bring volume to 100 ml with distilled water. Adjust pH to 7.0 with NaOH. Centrifuge the solution and filter-sterilize the supernatant. Store the solution under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere.       <br>
